Open source software eliminates licensing fees, making it a more affordable option for individuals and organizations with limited budgets.
The collaborative nature of open source development leads to faster bug fixes and feature improvements, enhancing long-term value.
Many large companies rely on open source software to reduce costs and increase efficiency, demonstrating its practical benefits in real-world applications.
Open source software promotes transparency and security, as the code is openly reviewed by a global community, reducing vulnerabilities.
By removing barriers to access, open source software enables broader participation in technology, fostering a more inclusive innovation ecosystem.